          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kuchen from Old High German kuohho from Proto-Germanic kōkô, \"cake\" — inherited; Dutch koek is the same word. (EtymDB 2.1) English cake is a cousin, through Norse."
            }
          ]
        },
